{"authored" [{"question" "q-124871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}2y\\,dx+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,dy+3z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=\\,i+t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ for $t\\in [1,3]?$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/review.json" "file_sha256" "71e372b8900659d39d9e18c3fedda5492bc8b8e62c82a5c3b8f9a58f6d758e07" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "93f77f44ca76f547a096a35ecb7aad38c805c7cf49fe3cdc40753d429e66bced" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/verification.json" "basis" 1883 "rationale" "The original source correctly substitutes 3t^2*(2t), then incorrectly simplifies it to6t^2. Correct pullback is6t^3 and integral120. Preserve the original prompt and four current distractor answer identities, replace the defective study alternative with the already stored correct exponent, new field identity with existing mathematically correct answer identity retained, preserve raw source and actual Correct probe grade as evidence."} {"question" "q-124871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along $C$, $x(t)=1$, $y(t)=t$, and $z(t)=t^2$, so $x'(t)=0$, $y'(t)=1$, and $z'(t)=2t$. Substitute both the coordinates and their derivatives:\n\n$$\\int_C 2y\\,dx+\\ln x\\,dy+3z\\,dz\n=\\int_1^3\\left(2t\\cdot0+\\ln(1)\\cdot1+3t^2\\cdot2t\\right)\\,dt\n=\\int_1^3 6t^3\\,dt.$$\n\nThus the equivalent integral is $\\int_1^3 6t^3\\,dt$, and its value is $[\\tfrac32t^4]_1^3=120$.\n\nThe original source accepted $\\int_1^3 6t^2\\,dt$ and its worked solution changed $3t^2\\cdot2t$ into $6t^2$. That simplification loses a factor of $t$. The study choice replaces that exponent with $3$; all other original choices are retained." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/review.json" "file_sha256" "71e372b8900659d39d9e18c3fedda5492bc8b8e62c82a5c3b8f9a58f6d758e07" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "93f77f44ca76f547a096a35ecb7aad38c805c7cf49fe3cdc40753d429e66bced" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/verification.json" "basis" 1883 "rationale" "The original source correctly substitutes 3t^2*(2t), then incorrectly simplifies it to6t^2. Correct pullback is6t^3 and integral120. Preserve the original prompt and four current distractor answer identities, replace the defective study alternative with the already stored correct exponent, new field identity with existing mathematically correct answer identity retained, preserve raw source and actual Correct probe grade as evidence."} {"question" "q-124871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{3}6t^{3}\\,dt"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/review.json" "file_sha256" "71e372b8900659d39d9e18c3fedda5492bc8b8e62c82a5c3b8f9a58f6d758e07" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "93f77f44ca76f547a096a35ecb7aad38c805c7cf49fe3cdc40753d429e66bced" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/verification.json" "basis" 1883 "rationale" "The original source correctly substitutes 3t^2*(2t), then incorrectly simplifies it to6t^2. Correct pullback is6t^3 and integral120. Preserve the original prompt and four current distractor answer identities, replace the defective study alternative with the already stored correct exponent, new field identity with existing mathematically correct answer identity retained, preserve raw source and actual Correct probe grade as evidence."}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-124871" []} "basis" 1883 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186177671 17592186177673 17592186177674 17592186177675 17592186232883] "immutable_fields" [[17592186336846 :answer-field/correct] [17592186336846 :answer-field/id] [17592186336846 :answer-field/key] [17592186336846 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
